---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import About from "../components/About.astro"
import AboutMe from "../components/AboutMe.astro"
import Cases from "../components/Cases.astro"
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro"
import Container from "../components/Container.astro"
import Cv from "../components/Cv.astro"
import Header from "../components/Header.astro"
import Main from "../components/Main.astro"

import CaseHogeschoolUtrecht from "../components/cases/HogeschoolUtrecht.astro"
import CaseQuaiDesNotaires from "../components/cases/QuaiDesNotaires.astro"
import CaseSamenOpStap from "../components/cases/SamenOpStap.astro"
import CaseSpeld from "../components/cases/Speld.astro"

import IconService from "../svgs/feature_service.svg"
---

<Base lang="en">
  <Header />
  <Main class="pitch">
    <About>
      <h1>Chessable &amp; Stef</h1>
      <p>
        I've spent most of my working life (15+) as a freelance full-stack
        developer. I've lead remote teams and I've worked on PHP/JS/React stacks
        for SaaS companies. As a freelancer I'm self-motivated and good at
        budgeting projects. I love your product and your vision and I think I'd
        be a great addition to your team.
      </p>
    </About>
    <Container>
      <section class="section">
        <p>
          I'm an on-again off-again chess player. My biggest achievement in
          chess is my win against{" "}
          <a href="https://twitter.com/blackatlantic">Geert</a>, who kept giving
          me hints that I should keep pushing my pawns. I was subscribed to{" "}
          <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC6hOVYvNn79Sl1Fc1vx2mYA">
            John's YouTube channel
          </a>{" "}
          at one time. I've even built a chess website, with just one blog post
          back in 2014:{" "}
          <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20150217122218/http://patzer.ch/analyze-your-games-with-a-chess-database-and-engine/">
            How to Analyse Your Games with a Chess Database and Engine
          </a>
          . Turns out I'm more of a system builder than a player.
        </p>

        <p>
          Originally from The Netherlands,{" "}
          <a href="https://lavalleedefretoy.com">
            I moved to France a couple of years ago
          </a>{" "}
          and I'm using <a href="https://apps.ankiweb.net/">Anki</a> to learn
          vocabulary. I'm even using Anki in a home-brew knowledge system. I've
          used spaced repetition for years and think it's a great idea to
          combine spaced repetion with chess learning.
        </p>

        <p>
          I've created an account and used your product, researched your current
          stack on <a href="https://www.wappalyzer.com">Wappalyzer</a> and read{" "}
          <a href="https://www.indiehackers.com/interview/chessable-3418ada3ff">
            David's Indie Hackers update
          </a>{" "}
          in which he calls himself more of a hacker than a developer. I get the
          feeling you have a legacy codebase on your hands and you're in the
          middle of a big reboot, I've done these before and I would love to
          help.
        </p>
      </section>
      <Cv />
      <Cases>
        <header>
          <IconService class="icon" />
          <h2>Relevant Projects</h2>
          <p>
            These are some of the projects I've done that are relevant to
            Chessable in some way. It could be because they showcase the tech
            stack{" "}
            <a href="https://www.chessable.com/careers/">
              you folks are looking for
            </a>
            , it might be because they're bigger projects with a lot of
            customers or visitors, or they might be projects where I've taken on
            lead roles.
          </p>
        </header>
        <CaseQuaiDesNotaires />
        <CaseHogeschoolUtrecht />
        <CaseSamenOpStap />
        <CaseSpeld />
      </Cases>
      <AboutMe />
      <Contact />
    </Container>
  </Main>
</Base>
